 I just have to do this  every day and if I don't I'm not gonna  beat myself up about it but I know very  well that if I don't do this every day  I'm further away from finishing  this software I want to finish and every  time I at least spend some time on it  and try to understand something that I'm  moving forward and that's that's good  I've also set a limit where well while  Classics been out for a while now and I  was addicted to Wow a long time ago when  I first came out and it was such a great  game and I so wanted to experience it  again but I didn't I just held back and  said look I just firmly told myself no  you're not getting a subscription unless  you finished this large chunk of code  and this thing this feature that I've  been stuck on from a little game engine  is the limiting factor here so when I do  finish it and when it does work good  I'll play some well but until then I  mean there's other games I can play that  aren't as addictive but if I get stuck  in the well rabbit hole or sucked into  the rabbit hole I know my heart's of  finishing this this software in a timely  manner are going to go down because well  I've learned from experience before I've  spent way too much time on well before  and you know it's fun it's a it's a  honestly well everyone's gonna have  varying opinions on this but I thought  it was a great life I absolutely loved  playing well back when it was and it's  prime for me I thought that was some of  the best experience of my life  I still have ten years later or however  long it's been - even more than that now  I still have real-life friends that I  made online from rating it Wow and  they're some of the coolest most  down-to-earth people I never would have  expected to meet otherwise and that's  that's something so I'm not bashing that  in any way although you know your  experience may vary because you know  there's people that didn't retain any  friends and played at a ton but that you  know it's just different for everyone it  depends what your goals are and if you  play a healer or not let's be real here  yeah that's that's probably why I made  friends it's cuz I played a healer and  when I started in you know people loved  healers give them all the gear to keep  me alive oh man we pulled too many stuff  and there's too much stuff and somehow  the healer kept us alive friend this guy  for life yeah it's that kind of stuff so  the important thing is to time box what  you're working on whether it's at work  or whether it's on your own stuff just  take everything that Forest Knight says  in his videos and I'll link it somewhere  maybe it'll be up here maybe will be  down there take that hall to heart  because it is it is so true and I really  wish that I saw that video earlier and  forest Knight if you see this video  thank you  that's uh something everybody needs to  know in here all right peace out you  guys see in the next video don't forget  to like to help this with the YouTube  algorithm and subscribe if you want to  see more content from me I'm gonna  continue making videos and make a lot of  tutorials some rants some talks try to  prepare people for the real world a  little bit help you advance and I really  really would like to do this more to do  that I have to get some support so  anything I can get I appreciate whether  it be it likes a sub a comment thank you  and I also do have a patreon and worked  on much yet but you are welcome to  donate and I will be doing something as  soon as I do get some donations I would  decided what I'm gonna do with it  there's just so many options so many  possibilities of things I could put in  there and do you know I gotta really  make sure I'm willing to do what I say  I'm gonna do a lot of people will say  we'll post our source code if you donate  so much and we'll do things every week  with some cert people credits at the end  of the video I don't know so I'm willing  to hear some opinions on what might work  there alright guys peace out see in the  next video take care of yourselves and  have a good day
 

